From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 17:11:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: pipeline commits by dropping the post-kickoff flush
 wait

msm_atomic_commit_tail() waited for the flush to complete immediately
after kicking off, and only then signalled hw_done and completed the
commit. Everything downstream of that wait therefore happened a full
transfer late:

 - drm_atomic_helper_wait_for_dependencies() holds the next nonblocking
   commit's tail work until this commit's hw_done, so the next frame
   could not even be programmed until this one had finished scanning
   out, and its kickoff slipped to the vblank after next;
 - complete_commit(), which is where the pageflip event is sent, ran at
   transfer end rather than at the point the hardware took ownership of
   the new frame.

On a command-mode panel the transfer occupies nearly the whole TE slot
(14.6 ms of 16.7 ms on a 1440x2880 DSC panel), so the two effects
compound and lock the session to half the panel rate: rock-steady
33.4 ms frame callbacks with an idle GPU and an idle compositor.

The wait buys nothing that is not already provided. commit_tail() opens
with the same wait_flush() before it touches any hardware, so a commit
can never program over an in-flight flush; and by the time flush_commit()
has returned, the CTL has latched, so the framebuffers being released by
the cleanup below are no longer referenced. Drop it and let commits
pipeline.

The async (legacy cursor) path keeps its wait: it has no wait_flush of
its own at the top, so two back-to-back async commits would have nothing
left ordering them.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_atomic.c | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_atomic.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_atomic.c
index 87a91148a731..854a272e9bdb 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_atomic.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_atomic.c
@@ -303,12 +303,14 @@ void msm_atomic_commit_tail(struct drm_atomic_state *state)
 	trace_msm_atomic_flush_commit(crtc_mask);
 	kms->funcs->flush_commit(kms, crtc_mask);
 	unlock_crtcs(kms, crtc_mask);
+
 	/*
-	 * Wait for flush to complete:
+	 * Deliberately no wait for the flush to complete here. The hardware
+	 * has latched this update, so the next commit is free to prepare the
+	 * one after it while this one is still being scanned out, and the
+	 * wait_flush at the top of the next commit_tail supplies the same
+	 * safety before anything is reprogrammed.
 	 */
-	trace_msm_atomic_wait_flush_start(crtc_mask);
-	kms->funcs->wait_flush(kms, crtc_mask);
-	trace_msm_atomic_wait_flush_finish(crtc_mask);
 
 	vblank_put(kms, crtc_mask);
 
